-- The hop of the electron along a link of doubled spin x from vertex v to vertex w (QSD V's Dirac term,
-- ψ†_w h_e ψ_v): v holds the electron as ((x v2) k, ½) kt with kt coupled to v's other two links, w is empty in
-- ((x w2) m) with m coupled to w's other two. The holonomy's spin ½ joins the link, x becomes x2 = x ± 1; at v the
-- electron's ½ is the holonomy's start, so v becomes the four-valent ((x2 v2) kt); at w the holonomy's end is the
-- electron's open index, so w becomes ((x2 w2) m2, ½) m with m2 = m ± 1. With normalized states the amplitude is
-- the product of the two recoupling coefficients: the edge's factor √((2x+1)/(2x2+1)) from D^x ⊗ D^½ = ⊕ D^x2 and
-- the factor √((2x2+1)/(2x+1)) of the map V_x → V_x2 ⊗ V_½ at w cancel.
hop-amp : List Bool → List Bool → List Bool → List Bool → List Bool → List Bool → List Bool → List Bool → Amp
hop-amp x x2 v2 k kt w2 m m2 = amp-mul (brecouple x x2 v2 k kt) (brecouple x2 x w2 m2 m)
